WEBVTT

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:35.990
<b>Sakura Feels a Pull at the Flower Viewing</b>

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:47.890
Oh, you're done with your bath, Sakura?

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:50.920
Yeah. You should have gone in with me.

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:55.080
I wanted to finish reading this. 
I'm so close to the end.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.290
Huh? This guy wasn't the culprit?

00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:01.910
But how? How? How? How?

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:05.070
Oh! That crack in the ceiling!

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:07.680
He went through there!

00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:11.680
Who could get through that? 
Just how flexible is he?

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:13.950
I don't believe it!

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:16.280
You were so sure you knew who it was.

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:17.940
So you were wrong, huh?

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:19.740
No! We don't know yet!

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:21.660
There could be a twist at the end!

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:24.490
No way! It's over!

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:29.520
That ain't right! Nobody's that flexible!

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:31.340
You're really upset about this, huh?

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:34.710
Spinny told me to read this book.

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:39.160
Then, at the two-thirds mark, 
there was a challenge from the author,

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:41.850
so we messaged each other with our 
guesses on who the culprit was.

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:44.150
And you guessed wrong?

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.050
What about Spinel-san?

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:49.940
He was right, wasn't he?

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:53.140
It was a fluke! He just got lucky!

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:56.530
Next time, we're gonna read 
a genre that I'm good at!

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:58.020
Like train tricks...

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:01.540
Do you like reading train timetables?

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:06.020
No, but goin' on trips and eatin' lots 
of yummy food is my specialty!

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:09.170
I don't think that has anything 
to do with solving mysteries...

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.130
<b>Rika-chan</b>

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:15.950
Hello, this is Sakura.

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:17.700
<i>Hi, this is Rika.</i>

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:18.830
Hi!

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:21.630
<i>About the flower-viewing party tomorrow...</i>

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:24.140
Yeah, I saw your message.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:26.000
<i>Sorry I can't make it.</i>

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:29.600
It's okay. You have a school event, right?

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:31.100
Yeah...

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:33.700
And on a weekend... That must be rough.

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:36.400
<i>It's in the afternoon, so it's not that bad.</i>

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:37.810
<i>I'm sad I can't go, though.</i>

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:42.450
Me, too. Sorry I couldn't plan it 
on a day when you'd be free.

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:45.000
<i>Don't worry about it. 
Invite me next time, okay?</i>

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:45.740
Sure!

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:47.110
<i>So, anyway,</i>

00:03:47.110 --> 00:03:50.300
<i>you joined the Cheerleading Club 
with Chiharu-chan again?</i>

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:51.380
Yeah!

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:53.790
<i>You should take some videos 
and send them to me!</i>

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:56.730
Sure! Send me more of your videos, too, okay?

00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:57.550
<i>Definitely.</i>

00:03:58.030 --> 00:03:59.700
<i>Well, I'll talk to you again soon.</i>

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:01.570
Okay, talk to you then.

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:04.960
One of your friends?

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:06.410
Yeah, Rika-chan.

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:08.340
Oh, the one who went to a 
different middle school.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:11.940
Yeah. The way she talks is much calmer now,

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:13.840
and she seems a lot more grown-up.

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:17.860
<b>Entrance Ceremony</b>

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:18.170
And she looked prettier than ever in the 
picture she sent of her new school uniform!

00:04:18.170 --> 00:04:20.600
She turned out the exact 
opposite of you, then!

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:26.870
I can't be like Rika-chan, but I'm 
slowly getting more grown-up!

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:30.320
You kick off your blanket and 
sleep hugging your pillow.

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:33.080
I don't think that's very grown-up...

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:34.160
Kero-chan!

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:37.430
Ya see? A grown-up wouldn't 
get mad over that, either.

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:43.800
Ugh! I'm not saving any of 
tomorrow's packed lunch for you!

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:48.090
Forgive me, Sakura-sama!

00:04:57.380 --> 00:04:59.620
The mini Hamburg steaks are done.

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:01.240
Thanks, Dad.

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:03.780
I'm glad it's good weather for 
viewing the cherry blossoms.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:04.520
I know.

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:08.170
The weather report said it'd be 
sunny, but I was still worried.

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:15.000
Must be because I'm always 
on my best behavior.

00:05:16.390 --> 00:05:19.280
Oh, bonito flakes? I like salmon better.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:23.070
There's still rice, so make some yourself!

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:25.730
Don't squeeze the rice 
so hard. It's too tough.

00:05:25.730 --> 00:05:27.640
All you ever do is complain!

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:30.160
Got any extras of those sides?

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:32.850
No problem. Do you need a lunch?

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:37.140
Yeah. My part-time job today doesn't 
offer lunch, so I'll take one.

00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:39.370
You can take one for Yukito-san, too!

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:41.110
I'll make the rice balls!

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:44.150
Are rice balls all you can make, monster?

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:45.680
I made the rolled omelets, too!

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:49.590
I am <i>not</i> a monster!

00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:51.060
Hey, it's me.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:51.660
I'm not!

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:54.880
I'm not a monster!

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:55.580
Sakura's making something.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.840
For you, too. For lunch.

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:01.840
No, Dad's making it with her. 
It should be safe.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:04.060
What's that supposed to mean?

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:04.710
<b>Yukito Tsukishiro</b>

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:06.550
Yuki wants to talk to you.

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:10.490
Hello?

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:13.230
<i>Sakura-chan? You're making lunch?</i>

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:15.030
<i>Yeah!</i>

00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:16.840
You don't mind making mine, too?

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:17.880
<i>Not at all!</i>

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:19.360
You'll have enough?

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:21.470
<i>If I come up short, I'll just 
put less in Onii-chan's.</i>

00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:26.120
<i>I'll take you up on that, then. 
I can't wait to eat it.</i>

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:29.020
<i>Sure! Good luck at work!</i>

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:30.110
Thanks.

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:32.820
I'll give it back to Onii-chan now.

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:40.910
Yuki said to thank you, too, Dad.

00:06:40.910 --> 00:06:43.460
Tell him to come visit again soon.

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:46.600
Hear that?

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:48.800
Okay. Later.

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:53.330
Let's do this!

00:06:57.590 --> 00:06:59.140
Hey, Onii-chan...

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:00.190
What?

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:02.970
How much has Yukito-san been eating, lately?

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:06.730
Not as much as he did when you 
were in elementary school...

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:10.250
But he still eats a lot for his size.

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:13.360
He hasn't been eating more again, lately?

00:07:15.230 --> 00:07:17.270
W-Well, it's spring, right?

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:21.120
Since it's warmer and the weather's nice, 
I thought he might get hungry...

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:24.880
Not really, no.

00:07:25.530 --> 00:07:26.640
I see.

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:33.300
<i>He used to eat a lot to make up 
for being short on magic,</i>

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:35.300
<i>but if that's not the case now...</i>

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:38.930
<i>I hope Yukito-san and Yue-san aren't having</i>

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:41.560
<i>any problems because of the new cards...</i>

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:43.580
Sakura-san.

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:47.950
Do you want the wieners 
bunny-shaped or octopus-shaped?

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:49.600
Bunnies would be great!

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:51.360
I'll do them with you.

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:52.780
Thanks.

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:54.970
Be careful with the knife, then.

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:55.720
I will.

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:01.840
That's it. You've gotten very good at that.

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:02.690
Really?

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:04.210
Yep, really.

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:08.080
Oh, and as for the vegetables... 
You'd prefer them grilled, right?

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:09.290
With squash, too?

00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:11.720
Yeah! I want to make buttered corn, too!

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:18.030
I'm heading out!

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:29.990
Take care out there.

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:31.200
Now, then!

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:38.280
I'm gonna have my flower-viewing 
lunch, while I watch TV!

00:08:42.260 --> 00:08:44.280
I'm so glad it's sunny...

00:08:44.990 --> 00:08:46.470
Tomoyo-chan!

00:08:48.030 --> 00:08:49.780
Hello, Sakura-chan.

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:51.990
I'm glad it's sunny today.

00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:52.740
Yeah!

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:56.320
It's too bad about Rika-chan.

00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:59.580
Yeah, but we're going to that movie, right?

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:02.690
The one Chiharu-chan and Naoko-chan 
said they wanted to see?

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:05.090
I thought I'd invite her to that.

00:09:05.590 --> 00:09:07.890
I hope it will fit in her schedule.

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:08.700
Yeah!

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:10.930
Is that your lunch?

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:14.680
Yeah. My dad helped me make it.

00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:17.400
The rolled omelets came out great this time!

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:19.710
I can't wait to try them.

00:09:19.710 --> 00:09:21.680
I made rice balls, too,

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:23.900
but my brother was being mean again.

00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:25.600
He said they were too hard.

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:28.380
And he was stealing bites, 
but then he said salmon would—

00:09:33.430 --> 00:09:35.100
Is something the matter?

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:38.000
No, nothing. Let's go.

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:49.320
Let's see... The others are...

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:50.820
Sakura-chan!

00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:52.820
There, they are!

00:09:54.370 --> 00:09:56.180
Sorry we're late!

00:09:56.180 --> 00:09:58.650
It's not even our meet-up time yet.

00:09:59.140 --> 00:10:01.420
You can put your shoes 
over there with the rest.

00:10:01.770 --> 00:10:03.510
Thank you.

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:15.320
Thank you for inviting me.

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:18.230
I'm glad you're here to see 
the flowers with us!

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:19.550
Where's Li-kun?

00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:22.380
He sent a message saying he'd be a bit late.

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:26.010
Hey, look at this. I made lemonade!

00:10:26.570 --> 00:10:28.640
I hope it tastes good.

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:31.140
Here.

00:10:31.140 --> 00:10:32.430
Thanks!

00:10:32.430 --> 00:10:33.910
Thank you.

00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:38.150
Well, now that Sakura-chan and 
Tomoyo-chan are here, let's toast.

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:41.560
Yeah. I'll do the speech—

00:10:41.560 --> 00:10:42.660
Cheers!

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:43.850
Cheers!

00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:47.010
It's great!

00:10:47.330 --> 00:10:48.650
It's delicious!

00:10:48.650 --> 00:10:50.170
I'm so glad.

00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:52.940
Should we wait for Li-kun before we eat?

00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:54.770
He said we can start without him.

00:10:54.770 --> 00:10:58.330
He might feel bad if we wait for him.

00:10:58.330 --> 00:11:00.360
Let's just eat really slowly.

00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:01.660
Yeah.

00:11:01.660 --> 00:11:03.300
Okay, let's get started.

00:11:06.830 --> 00:11:07.460
Here.

00:11:07.460 --> 00:11:08.660
Thanks.

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:11.860
Yamazaki-kun made the 
lunches for you two, today?

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:14.870
Yeah. I was in charge of snacks and drinks.

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:17.510
Do you like to cook?

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:21.560
Hmm... If I had to say, 
I guess I like it well enough.

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:24.380
I see it as an experiment, 
more than anything.

00:11:25.070 --> 00:11:26.250
An experiment?

00:11:26.670 --> 00:11:30.830
Like, what would happen if I added 
this seasoning with this seasoning?

00:11:30.830 --> 00:11:34.010
Or, if I did this to this ingredient, 
what would it transform into?

00:11:34.350 --> 00:11:35.760
Transform...

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:42.090
Sometimes, things end up in his 
lunches that I don't even recognize.

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:43.650
That sounds like fun!

00:11:46.380 --> 00:11:48.560
Akiho-chan, your lunch looks so pretty!

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:50.060
It does!

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:52.550
The colors are lovely, 
and it looks delicious, too.

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:53.330
Did you make it?

00:11:53.660 --> 00:11:55.570
No, it was made for me!

00:11:55.570 --> 00:11:57.940
I'm not good with my hands at all...

00:11:57.940 --> 00:12:01.160
Are you living with someone here in Japan?

00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:02.700
Or do you live alone?

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:07.050
I live with someone who's taken 
care of me since I was little.

00:12:07.050 --> 00:12:08.140
Family?

00:12:08.140 --> 00:12:11.190
No, we're not related...

00:12:13.490 --> 00:12:15.070
But it's someone important to me.

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:17.320
Akiho-chan...

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:20.380
You really love that person, don't you?

00:12:20.740 --> 00:12:21.590
Huh?

00:12:21.930 --> 00:12:24.100
You said that with such a 
gentle look on your face.

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:25.860
H-Huh?

00:12:26.670 --> 00:12:29.890
Do you guys want to trade 
sides from our lunches?

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:31.980
All right. That sounds wonderful.

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:34.690
I made yakisoba for mine.

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:36.220
For a packed lunch?

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:39.490
I read about a way to make it, 
so it's good, even when cold.

00:12:39.800 --> 00:12:44.110
I wanted to try it out as 
practice for my next play.

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:46.010
There's yakisoba in your play?

00:12:46.010 --> 00:12:48.980
Yeah. I wanted to make 
it as part of the play.

00:12:48.980 --> 00:12:50.980
Eat some of mine, too.

00:12:50.980 --> 00:12:52.120
My special for today is...

00:12:52.650 --> 00:12:54.210
Octopus ball-style squid balls!

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:56.210
Are they octopus or squid?

00:13:15.880 --> 00:13:18.270
This rolled omelet is delicious!

00:13:18.580 --> 00:13:20.060
I'm so glad!

00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:23.520
The sandwiches from your 
lunch are really good, too!

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:26.630
Yamazaki-kun's squid balls 
are pretty tasty, too.

00:13:26.630 --> 00:13:28.520
Especially with the cheese on top.

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:31.110
It's a secret ingredient.

00:13:31.110 --> 00:13:33.240
There's nothing secret about it!

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:55.260
Is something wrong?

00:13:55.800 --> 00:13:59.030
It felt like someone was 
pulling me from behind.

00:13:59.300 --> 00:14:00.670
I was just imagini—

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:03.860
Sakura-chan?

00:14:09.600 --> 00:14:12.490
U-Um, I just... Phone call!

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:14.010
I need to make a phone call!

00:14:16.810 --> 00:14:18.020
Sakura-chan?

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:25.580
W-Wait a second!

00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:37.820
Where are you trying to take me?

00:14:37.820 --> 00:14:39.360
Is it another card?

00:14:54.770 --> 00:14:55.570
That's...

00:15:04.010 --> 00:15:05.130
I'm gonna crash into it!

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:07.450
<i>Release!</i>

00:15:21.150 --> 00:15:22.010
<i>Siege!</i>

00:15:26.080 --> 00:15:28.060
Make yourself more flexible!

00:15:31.460 --> 00:15:33.440
It didn't work... I'm still being pulled.

00:15:34.460 --> 00:15:36.200
Show me what lies in front of you!

00:15:42.910 --> 00:15:45.840
<i>I'm being pulled toward
that cherry blossom tree.</i>

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:49.480
<i>If this is the work of a card, 
that's where it must be!</i>

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:53.430
<i>But I can't do anything like this.</i>

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:55.090
<i>I need to get closer.</i>

00:15:57.860 --> 00:16:01.360
<i>But if I undo my magic and 
crash into the tree...</i>

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:07.530
<i>It'll be all right. Relax.</i>

00:16:07.530 --> 00:16:09.220
<i>Keep looking forward!</i>

00:16:10.980 --> 00:16:11.620
Now, go!

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:20.320
There, it is!

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:30.670
<i>Force without master,</i>

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:33.840
<i>heed the call of my Staff of Dreams, 
and become my power!</i>

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:36.510
<i>Secure!</i>

00:16:57.100 --> 00:16:58.540
I made it in time!

00:16:59.530 --> 00:17:01.520
Gravitation...

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:06.540
<b>Gravity</b>

00:17:03.780 --> 00:17:05.320
"Gravity."

00:17:09.970 --> 00:17:10.840
Hello?

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:12.790
<i>Are you all right, Sakura-chan?</i>

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:16.050
Yeah. Sorry I worried you.

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:17.910
It was a card, after all.

00:17:24.740 --> 00:17:26.480
<i>Is something wrong?</i>

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:28.570
Sorry. I'm fine.

00:17:29.590 --> 00:17:30.560
Hey, listen...

00:17:43.070 --> 00:17:44.750
It's so beautiful.

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:48.830
I didn't know such a big cherry 
blossom tree was here.

00:17:48.830 --> 00:17:51.040
I guess it's what you'd call 
a well-kept secret.

00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:54.690
You'd think everyone would 
talk about a tree this big.

00:17:54.930 --> 00:17:58.360
Lucky for us, it's a spot where 
flower-viewing parties are allowed.

00:17:58.360 --> 00:18:00.670
Thanks for finding it, Sakura-chan.

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:05.210
What's wrong, Tomoyo-chan?

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:09.680
I missed the chance to film 
your heroic deeds again.

00:18:10.490 --> 00:18:14.700
Perhaps I need to undergo a purification...

00:18:17.160 --> 00:18:18.320
Oh, there he is.

00:18:22.980 --> 00:18:24.340
Li-kun!

00:18:24.340 --> 00:18:26.060
Sorry I'm late.

00:18:26.060 --> 00:18:27.720
No worries.

00:18:27.720 --> 00:18:29.420
Did you find the place okay?

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:30.360
Yeah.

00:18:32.940 --> 00:18:36.190
Looks like you went ahead 
and started. Thanks.

00:18:36.730 --> 00:18:38.180
Did you have lunch, Li-kun?

00:18:38.770 --> 00:18:40.170
Yeah, I did.

00:18:42.570 --> 00:18:45.260
I brought these for you guys.

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:48.100
Wow, Li-kun's peach buns!

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:49.140
I missed these!

00:18:49.490 --> 00:18:53.080
Syaoran-kun makes really good sweets.

00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:54.640
Try some, Akiho-chan.

00:18:54.980 --> 00:18:56.670
Thank you!

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:01.710
It's delicious!

00:19:01.710 --> 00:19:02.820
You like it?

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:06.460
And you made them yourself? 
That's amazing!

00:19:06.460 --> 00:19:08.160
It's not that difficult.

00:19:08.620 --> 00:19:10.460
Oh, no. All of the things

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:14.380
that everyone has made are truly delicious.

00:19:14.760 --> 00:19:16.420
I need to work much harder.

00:19:16.650 --> 00:19:18.560
I can teach you how to make sweets.

00:19:18.560 --> 00:19:20.000
I can teach experimental cooking.

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:21.760
Just teach her how to do it normally.

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:23.760
Thank you!

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:27.680
You know, "sweets" got their name because 
a certain guest at an upper-class tea party

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:29.890
said something very sweet...

00:19:29.030 --> 00:19:30.330
Did something happen?

00:19:31.110 --> 00:19:32.540
There was another card...

00:19:33.030 --> 00:19:34.820
I'll fill you in later.

00:19:34.820 --> 00:19:36.020
Well, that, too...

00:19:36.300 --> 00:19:41.790
But when I said I'd already had 
lunch, you looked kind of sad.

00:19:42.670 --> 00:19:45.030
S-Sorry! Don't worry about that!

00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:47.400
I have to, when it's about you.

00:19:48.810 --> 00:19:50.290
W-Well...

00:19:51.020 --> 00:19:55.200
I made you a lunch, like I was 
saying on the phone...

00:19:55.720 --> 00:19:59.650
But don't worry about it. I'll give it 
to Kero-chan when I get home.

00:19:59.990 --> 00:20:01.840
I'll make you another one, sometime.

00:20:03.440 --> 00:20:05.830
Can I have that one?

00:20:05.830 --> 00:20:07.100
B-But...

00:20:07.880 --> 00:20:08.630
I want to eat it.

00:20:09.020 --> 00:20:12.160
You don't have to force it! 
You said you already ate...

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:13.980
I'll be fine. I want to eat it.

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:14.850
But, but...

00:20:15.550 --> 00:20:16.610
I can't?

00:20:16.840 --> 00:20:19.340
N-No, you can...

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:25.110
But really, don't force it.

00:20:28.530 --> 00:20:29.820
Time to eat.

00:20:33.160 --> 00:20:34.170
It's great.

00:20:39.650 --> 00:20:42.380
Rolled omelets make you 
think of Castella, right?

00:20:42.870 --> 00:20:46.650
Castella was originally made 
using cast-off crumbs.

00:20:46.650 --> 00:20:49.970
Just like how "offal" got its name from 
the "off-fall" during butchering.

00:20:49.970 --> 00:20:52.770
As for where the -tella part came from...

00:20:52.770 --> 00:20:56.520
Priests at a temple would "tell-a 
friend," or another priest,

00:20:56.520 --> 00:20:59.070
when they had leftover sweets, 
so they'd make Castella together.

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:01.110
And it was delicious!

00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:03.320
It made the temple so rich,

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:06.890
they built additional buildings and 
even had branches. It was crazy!

00:21:06.890 --> 00:21:09.160
Why would a temple have branches?

00:21:09.160 --> 00:21:10.650
I had no idea!

00:21:10.650 --> 00:21:14.410
It seems like Yamazaki-kun will take 
any opening he can find, lately.

00:21:14.700 --> 00:21:16.850
I'm already full.

00:21:16.850 --> 00:21:19.570
I haven't gotten to the temple's 
global expansion yet. You see—

00:21:19.570 --> 00:21:21.300
I want to hear Tomoyo-chan sing!

00:21:21.540 --> 00:21:22.670
Me, too!

00:21:24.340 --> 00:21:25.460
Me, too.

00:21:25.460 --> 00:21:28.050
Tomoyo-san, will you sing for us?

00:21:28.420 --> 00:21:30.280
If it's all right with everyone.

00:21:37.460 --> 00:21:44.000
<i>The sky is watching</i>

00:21:44.440 --> 00:21:51.120
<i>As you begin to dream</i>

00:21:51.120 --> 00:22:00.120
<i>Reach out to the tomorrow 
You can see through it</i>

00:22:01.130 --> 00:22:07.520
<i>All you have to do is smile</i>

00:22:07.970 --> 00:22:14.390
<i>And you can change this world</i>

00:22:14.820 --> 00:22:21.740
<i>The interfering voices and the 
clouds darkening your heart</i>

00:22:21.740 --> 00:22:28.830
<i>Will all clear away</i>

00:24:10.150 --> 00:24:12.360
Hidey-howdy-ho!

00:24:11.590 --> 00:24:12.970
<b>Leave It to Kero-chan!</b>

00:24:12.960 --> 00:24:17.430
We're back with the oasis for your 
heart, "Leave It to Kero-chan!"

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:16.180
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:16.180
<b>K</b>

00:24:16.180 --> 00:24:17.430
<b>Do you have to say stuff 
like that every time?!</b>

00:24:17.430 --> 00:24:22.690
<b>K</b>

00:24:17.430 --> 00:24:22.690
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:17.750 --> 00:24:22.680
Today, we'll be lookin' at the lunches Sakura 
and her friends ate at their flower viewing!

00:24:22.930 --> 00:24:24.730
Don't they all look tasty?

00:24:24.730 --> 00:24:27.850
Akiho's looks amazing! 
Did she make it herself?

00:24:27.850 --> 00:24:31.190
I wish I could've shared it with them, 
under that cherry blossom tree...

00:24:31.200 --> 00:24:32.200
<b>Take me, too!</b>

00:24:32.190 --> 00:24:34.870
Sometimes, y'all find yourselves 
drawn to things, too, right?

00:24:32.200 --> 00:24:37.280
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:32.200 --> 00:24:37.280
<b>K</b>

00:24:34.870 --> 00:24:38.030
When that happens, it's okay 
to just go with the flow!

00:24:38.030 --> 00:24:39.990
Ta-ta!

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:41.870
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:24:40.290 --> 00:24:42.350
Strange things keep happening,

00:24:42.350 --> 00:24:45.150
but I'm so happy I get to see Akiho-chan!

00:24:45.150 --> 00:24:48.510
Come to think of it, I wonder 
which club Akiho-chan will join...

00:24:48.500 --> 00:24:55.010
<b>Sakura, the Rabbit, and the Song of the Moon</b>

00:24:48.880 --> 00:24:51.870
Next time, "Sakura, the Rabbit, 
and the Song of the Moon."

00:24:52.180 --> 00:24:54.760
Say it with me: "Release!"

00:24:55.010 --> 00:25:00.010
<b>End</b>
